  "globalInvariants": [
    "Tenant comes only from the authenticated context; a body tenant is rejected.",
    "Self scope is principal-to-person-to-worker-to-relationship-to-assignment and requires explicit selection when more than one effective context exists.",
    "Every owner reference is tenant, schema, public ID, revision, digest, purpose, population, field-policy and as-of checked; missing, stale, revoked, cross-tenant or wrong-entity refs produce zero writes.",
    "Public business UUIDs use the owner transaction allocator; correlation, idempotency, digest, array order and first-match selection never create or substitute identity.",
    "All business effective intervals are half-open; civil dates remain civil dates and instants carry an explicit IANA timezone/DST decision where local time matters.",
    "Every mutation uses expected aggregate version and pre-state, immutable input/source artifact, atomic receipt/audit/outbox, and response IDs/versions/states from actual RETURNING values.",
    "No module reads or writes another owner's database. Cross-owner data is accepted only through the registered DTO/SPI snapshot or minimized event then refetched.",
    "Optional capability absence cannot break unrelated core; a journey that declares a required owner blocks with zero effects when that owner is unavailable.",
    "Published or financially closed facts are corrected by superseding/correction/reversal records, never destructive update/delete or history rewrite.",
    "Company policy is versioned tenant configuration, country law is an optional signed pack, and executable scripts/SQL/JAR/shell/customer branching are forbidden."
  ],
